{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Çengelhan Rahmi M. Koç Museum (Turkish: "Çengelhan Rahmi M. Koç Müzesi" ) is a technology museum in Ankara, Turkey.","title":"Çengelhan Rahmi M. Koç Museum"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Rahmi M. Koç Museum is a private industrial museum in Istanbul, Turkey dedicated to history of transport, industry and communications.","title":"Rahmi M. Koç Museum"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Rahmi M. Koç, member of the wealthiest dynasty in Turkey and retired boss of the Koç Group, founded the museum in 1991, which was opened on December 13, 1994.","title":"Rahmi M. Koç Museum"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The museum is located in the suburb of Hasköy on the north shore of the Golden Horn and situated in two historical buildings connected to each other.","title":"Rahmi M. Koç Museum"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It is open to public every day except Monday.","title":"Rahmi M. Koç Museum"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The museum's general manager is Ertuğrul Duru.","title":"Rahmi M. Koç Museum"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Milion (Greek: Μίλιον or Μίλλιον , "Míllion"; Turkish: "Milyon taşı" ) was a monument erected in the early 4th century AD in Constantinople (modern-day Istanbul, Turkey).","title":"Milion"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was the Byzantine zero-mile marker, the starting-place for the measurement of distances for all the roads leading to the cities of the Byzantine Empire.","title":"Milion"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It thus served the same function as the Golden Milestone ("Milliarium Aureum ") in Rome's forum.","title":"Milion"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The domed building of the Milion rested on four large arches, and it was expanded and decorated with several statues and paintings.","title":"Milion"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" It survived the Ottoman conquest of Constantinople in 1453 but had disappeared by the start of the 16th century.","title":"Milion"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" During excavations in the 1960s, some partial fragments of it were discovered under houses in the area.","title":"Milion"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Rahmi Mustafa Koç (born in 1930 in Ankara), is a Turkish businessman and philanthropist.","title":"Rahmi Koç"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" In 2016, Forbes ranked him #906 richest person in the world with a net worth of $2.6 billion.","title":"Rahmi Koç"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 2013, he is the Turkish person who paid the most income taxes in his country, totalling 37.5 million liras.","title":"Rahmi Koç"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Children's Museum, Siri Fort, established by the Archaeological Survey of India (ASI) is a museum specifically created to educate children on the cultural, archaeological and historical heritage of India through replicated sculptures created from the existing well known sculptures in various museums and heritage sites in the country.","title":"Children's Museum, Siri Fort"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The museum houses 30 such sculptures created by students of the College of Arts and Crafts, Patna, under the direction of K. K. Mohammed, an archaeologist who had formerly worked as Superintendent Archaeologist of ASI's Delhi circle.","title":"Children's Museum, Siri Fort"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The museum is located in a lane adjoining the Siri Fort Auditorium and Siri Fort sports complex in South Delhi, New Delhi.","title":"Children's Museum, Siri Fort"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" A unique life-size sculpture created and exhibited in the museum is of Mughal Emperor Akbar which is not found any where else in the country.","title":"Children's Museum, Siri Fort"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" There are also statues of Emperor Ashoka, and Shah Jahan; these three statues were added when the museum was opened for public viewing in May 2011 and are located in the garden surrounding the museum.","title":"Children's Museum, Siri Fort"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Mongolian Natural History Museum (Mongolian: Байгалийн түүхийн музей ) is a repository and research institution located in Ulaanbaatar, Mongolia.","title":"Mongolian Natural History Museum"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The museum was previously known as the Mongolian National Museum or State Central Museum.","title":"Mongolian Natural History Museum"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" This change in name has often led to confusion with Ulaanbaatar's other preeminent museum, the National Museum of Mongolia.","title":"Mongolian Natural History Museum"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Although the two museums are located quite close to one another, they contain very different exhibits.","title":"Mongolian Natural History Museum"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The Mongolian National Museum focuses on the archaeology and history of Mongolia, while the Mongolian Natural History Museum is concerned primarily with the flora, fauna, geology and natural history of the country.","title":"Mongolian Natural History Museum"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Yes
